SUMMARY:Join Cho for a Hike in Silver Creek Conservation Area
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\nMeetUp Location: Free roadsid
 e/street parking along Fallbrook Trail and Side Road 27 (no formal\, large
  designated parking lot).\n\nLocated in Silver Creek Conservation Area nea
 r Halton Hills\, this complex network traverses one of the most ecological
 ly diverse sections of the Niagara Escarpment. Historically\, this area wa
 s settled by the Bennett family and later protected to preserve the Credit
  River headwaters. Geologically\, the Great Esker trail follows a rare gla
 cial ridge of sand and gravel formed by a meltwater river under ancient ic
 e. The forest is a lush mix of sugar maple and hemlock\, home to white-tai
 led deer and spotted salamanders. The terrain is technical and rugged\, fe
 aturing steep rocky inclines\, limestone crevices\, and muddy lowland sect
 ions. Hikers recommend waterproof boots for the Silver Creek crossings and
  mention the esker provides unique elevated views.\n**11.4kmLength Loop**\
 n**177mElevation gain**\n**Wear hiking boots please! It can get muddy here
 .**
