SUMMARY:Barbecue and Hike through Tommy Thompson Park.
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\nLocation: Meet at the entranc
 e of Tommy Thompson Park -Leslie Street Spit\n**It's time to have some fun
 !**\nWhat better way to celebrate the end of Summer with a barbecue by the
  lake. Join us for burgers and drinks **under the tents** and on the water
  at Ashbridges Bay for burgers and drinks!\n($10. For a burger and drink.)
 \nAfter a 8km hike (with some fun things happening along the way) at Tommy
  Thompson Park we will head to Ashbridges Bay for burgers- veggie and meat
 .\nFeel free to bring alcoholic beverages\, and board games - We will have
  a beach ball.\n\nTommy Thompson Park is a man-made urban wilderness and w
 ildlife sanctuary built on the Leslie Street Spit\, stretching 5 kilometer
 s to Lake Ontario.\nManaged by the Toronto and Region Conservation Authori
 ty\, this unique park offers a peaceful escape from the city with a mix of
  wetlands\, meadows\, and trails.\nA unique place near downtown Toronto to
  experience nature\, and *one of the best places for bird-watching in the 
 city*\, with more than 300 recorded species!
