SUMMARY:Devils Hole - US Side
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\nMeetup: **Niagara Gorge - US 
 side**\nMeet up point: Devil's Hole State Park Parking Area\nAddress: 5100
  Niagara Scenic Pkwy\, Niagara Falls\, NY 14305\, United States\nGPS Coord
 inates: 43.13301222763603\, -79.04771831578047 (or 43°07'58.8"N 79°02'51
 .8"W)\n**Make sure you have your passport!**\nWe usually hike the Canadian
  side\, so we decided we needed a different point of view!\nDevil’s Hole
  is a semi-circular notch formed by an ancient waterfall draining a sectio
 n of Glacial Lake Tonawanda. This waterfall formed as the main Falls erode
 d back past this point in the gorge. Lake Tonawanda eventually dried up al
 ong with its waterfall.\nIn the early 1700's\, the raging waters so terrif
 ied the locals that it was supposed that the devil lived there. The name s
 tuck.\n**Legend and Lore of Devil’s Hole**\n**Devil’s Hole Massacre:**
  On September 14\, 1763\, a British supply train of wagons was passing by 
 Devil’s Hole when a band of Senecas ambushed the party\, killing all but
  a few who escaped (2 or 3). The commotion was heard by soldiers stationed
  near the head of the Portage in Lewiston and reinforcements were sent mar
 ching up the road in formation. These troops were also attacked and basica
 lly wiped out.
